The loadout is correct (truncated head but shows mage/cleric/paladin; warrior likely as before). Now run a 30s probe collecting spell names and damage/heal numbers. I need to ensure the page is on warrior and the game is running. The class changes reset player stats but the game continues. Let me run the probe.

Probe script:
```
async (page) => {
  const names = new Set(['Apocalipsis','Juicio Final','Ráfaga Ígnea','Sanar','Castigo Divino','Fuente de vida','Inmovilizar','Remover parálisis']);
  const seen = {};
  const damages = [];
  const heals = [];
  const statuses = {};
  for (let i=0;i<300;i++) {
    const s = await page.evaluate(() => window.AO_DEBUG());
    for (const t of s.texts) {
      if (names.has(t)) seen[t] = (seen[t]||0)+1;
      const d = /^-(\d+)$/.exec(t); if (d) damages.push(+d[1]);
      const h = /^\+(\d+)$/.exec(t); if (h) heals.push(+h[1]);
      if (['Paralizado','Removida','ERRADO','esquivó','falló'].includes(t)) statuses[t]=(statuses[t]||0)+1;
    }
    await page.waitForTimeout(100);
  }
  const sum = a => a.reduce((x,y)=>x+y,0);
  return {seconds:30, seen, statuses, damage: {n:damages.length,min:Math.min(...damages),max:Math.max(...damages),avg:+(sum(damages)/damages.length).toFixed(1)}, heals:{n:heals.length,min:Math.min(...heals),max:Math.max(...heals),avg:+(sum(heals)/heals.length).toFixed(1)}};
}
```

But floating text dedupe: `AO_DEBUG().texts` returns the current floating texts each sample; the same text persists ~1s, so counts are inflated. That's okay for presence. Damage min/max: the damage values include melee 85-105, spells 90-144, potion heals etc. We can filter by pairing? Not easily. But we can check max damage 144 and presence of new spell names.

Note: The game may have been running for a while and some fighters may be dead/respawning. It's an endless arena; fine.

Also, the class UI switch reset player to warrior at the end (we set warrior). Good.

